      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this makes sense as a quick fix.\n\nSome ideas perhaps for a later CL:\n1) I\u0027m curious why we end up going through pe_invalidate_explicit_contract while disconnected. Would it make sense to avoid making that call?\n2) Alternatively, could tweak typec_update_cc to be smarter and do the right thing based on connected/disconnected (since we already cache values to apply later)?\n3) Add a unit test?\n",
      "revId": "a622de783225de0567a37d89da22c81b202abe5d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba64fe82_568bb8d3",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1287197
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-22T21:04:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1.  We\u0027ve made pe_invalidate_explicit_contract part of our PD_DISCONNECTED hook, so I think we need it to cover ourselves both in the event of an unplug and in case of a forced role change (ex. going from sourcing to sink-only).  The flag clear isn\u0027t super important for disconnect because we\u0027ll be clearing out all flags anyway next connection, but disabling FRS is important. \n\n2.  Currently, typec_update_cc() is used both outside the TC and within the TC whenever we want to update the CC lines.  So it we wanted to gate it on connected, then I think we\u0027d need to make the PE and PRL their own API to call, which is a doable option.\n\n3.  Yup, I probably could/should write a unit test...",
      "parentUuid": "fd67760a_746ceea2",
      "revId": "a622de783225de0567a37d89da22c81b202abe5d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
